{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:53:31+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "9cb7492188c8bd799f9c57e49bb8875a", "span_id": "3f2f5e5920d49b6b", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "7A3DF87F", "msg": "{'role': 'assistant', 'parts': [{'type': 'tool_call', 'id': 'fc_b76203f9-0ce2-48bb-8f7f-c48c11cf9c84', 'name': 'query_knowledge_base', 'arguments': '{\"question\":\"Model validation requirements in FAB Model Risk Management (MRM) framework: documentation, testing, governance, sign‑off criteria.\"}'}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:53:31+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "9cb7492188c8bd799f9c57e49bb8875a", "span_id": "3f2f5e5920d49b6b", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "7A3DF87F", "msg": "{'role': 'tool', 'parts': [{'type': 'tool_call_response', 'id': 'fc_b76203f9-0ce2-48bb-8f7f-c48c11cf9c84', 'response': \"Based on the First Abu Dhabi Bank (FAB) Model Risk Management (MRM) Framework and the Central Bank of the UAE (CBUAE) Circular No. 2024/BSE/047, the model validation requirements are structured across documentation, testing, governance, and sign-off criteria as follows:\\n\\n### 1. Documentation Requirements\\nFAB requires a comprehensive **Model Evidence Pack (MEP)** for all Tier 1 (High) and Tier 2 (Medium) models. This serves as the primary audit document and must include:\\n*   **Model Overview & Design:** Unique model ID, theoretical basis, mathematical formulation, and assumptions/limitations [FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Section 3.1].\\n*   **Data Documentation:** Full data dictionary, data lineage from source to model input, data quality assessments, and training period details [FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Section 3.1; CBUAE Circular, Article 3.1.2].\\n*   **Validation Record:** Independent validation findings, identified weaknesses, management responses, and outstanding remediation actions [FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Section 3.1].\\n*   **Performance Metrics:** Results of in-sample and out-of-sample testing, benchmarking against challenger models, and cross-validation [FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Section 3.1].\\n*   **Human Override Record:** Trend analysis of human override rates for the preceding 12 months [FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Section 3.1].\\n\\nAdditionally, FAB must maintain a centralized **AI Model Inventory** tracking deployment dates, ownership, validation status, and risk classifications [CBUAE Circular, Article 2.2.1].\\n\\n### 2. Testing Requirements\\nTesting is strictly tied to the model's risk tier and use-case:\\n*   **Methodological Testing:** Validation must include replication of the model's development methodology, sensitivity analysis, and assessment of conceptual soundness [CBUAE Circular, Article 3.2.2].\\n*   **Performance Benchmarking:** Models must be benchmarked against alternative approaches, challenger models, or expert judgment [FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Section 3.1; CBUAE Circular, Article 3.2.2].\\n*   **Pricing-Specific Testing:** For AI/ML models used in credit pricing, additional testing is required to assess:\\n    *   Pricing floor and floor compliance mechanisms [CBUAE Circular, Article 3.2.3].\\n    *   Human oversight control effectiveness [CBUAE Circular, Article 3.2.3].\\n    *   Model behavior under **stressed market conditions** [CBUAE Circular, Article 3.2.3].\\n*   **Data Input Testing:** Interest rate/FTP and risk rating data used in pricing models must be verified against authorized internal systems without undocumented manual overrides [CBUAE Circular, Article 7.1.2].\\n\\n### 3. Governance Requirements\\n*   **Board & Executive Oversight:** The Board must review and approve an **AI Governance Policy** annually. An AI Risk Officer (at minimum a CRO-level executive) is designated to oversee implementation [CBUAE Circular, Article 2.1.1 & 2.1.2].\\n*   **Independent Validation Separation:** Validation must be performed by a function organizationally separate from the model development team [CBUAE Circular, Article 3.2.1].\\n*   **Human\"}]}"}
