g cross-sell revenues and the overall relationship RAROC.\\n* **Endorsement:** Confirmation that the request has been reviewed and endorsed by the Head of Credit Pricing. **[Source: FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4 · Section 6.1]**\\n\\n### 4. Pricing Exception Approval Hierarchy\\nThe required approval authority is determined by the severity of the pricing deviation (basis points below floor) or the resulting RAROC.\\n\\n| Exception Category | Pricing Deviation / RAROC | Required Approval Authority |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Minor** | Up to **15 bps** below floor | Segment Credit Head |\\n| **Standard** | **15–40 bps** below floor | Country Credit Committee (CCC) |\\n| **Major** | **40–80 bps** below floor | Group Credit Committee (GCC) |\\n| **Strategic** | **>80 bps** below floor **OR** RAROC < **8%** | Chief Commercial Officer (CCO) & Chief Risk Officer (CRO) |\\n\\n*Note: Executing a transaction below the established floor rates without the appropriate Pricing Exception constitutes a violation of bank policy and is subject to disciplinary action.* **[Source: FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4 · Section 6.2]**\"}]}"}
