{"ts": "2026-06-29T14:59:44+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "6321fb9e6b271fed80062db6a0a2454c", "span_id": "c0d8280e0e985019", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "3EA99AC3", "msg": "{'role': 'tool', 'parts': [{'type': 'tool_call_response', 'id': 'fc_497f4fbc-4b06-4629-9242-8ee53ba30c1c', 'response': \"Based on the **FAB Credit Pricing Policy (v2.4)**, the standard minimum pricing floors for A-rated Corporate Term Loans are set as the following spreads over the applicable Funds Transfer Pricing (FTP) rate, based on the facility's contractual tenor:\\n\\n* **Tenor ≤ 1 Year:** 85 bps over FTP\\n* **Tenor 1-3 Years:** 105 bps over FTP\\n* **Tenor 3-5 Years:** 130 bps over FTP\\n* **Tenor > 5 Years:** 165 bps over FTP\\n\\n**Additional Policy Notes:**\\n* **Source:** `FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4`, Section 3.1, Table 3.1 (*Corporate Term Loans*).\\n* **Relationship Value Adjustment:** Per Section 2.4, the required margin may be reduced by **up to 25 bps** from these standard floors if the client demonstrates documented cross-sell revenues exceeding AED 500,000 per annum, subject to credit authority approval and annual review.\\n* **Pricing Exceptions:** Any pricing below these floors (after adjustments) requires a formally documented Pricing Exception approved at the relevant authority level (Section 6).\\n* **FTP Reference:** Ensure you pull the current matched-maturity AED FTP rate from the Treasury portal at the time of term sheet issuance, as FTP rates are updated monthly.\"}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-06-29T14:59:44+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "6321fb9e6b271fed80062db6a0a2454c", "span_id": "c0d8280e0e985019", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "3EA99AC3", "msg": "{'role': 'assistant', 'parts': [{'type': 'text', 'content': '**Deal‑specific figures for CUST002 (Falcon Steel Industries)** – *source: query_structured_data*  \\n\\n| Field | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| deal_id | DEAL005 |\\n| deal_date | 2025‑10‑24 00:00:00 |\\n| customer_id | CUST002 |\\n| customer_name | Falcon Steel Industries |\\n| customer_segment | Corporate |\\n| region | Abu Dhabi |\\n| risk_category | Low |\\n| internal_rating | A |\\n| product_id | PROD002 |\\n| product_type | Loan |\\n| currency | AED |\\n| tenor | 12M |\\n| requested_amount | 58,000,000 |\\n| funding_cost_pct | 5.55% |\\n| risk_premium_pct | 0.1% |\\n| relationship_discount_pct | 0.45% |\\n| recommended_price_pct | 7.3% |\\n| final_approved_price_pct | 7.25% |\\n| expected_margin_pct | 1.35% |\\n| deal_outcome | Won |\\n| benchmark_rate_pct_treasury | 5.35% |\\n| funding_cost_pct_treasury | 5.55% |\\n| net_margin_pct | 1.15% |\\n| spread_over_benchmark_pct | 1.9% |\\n| margin_vs_recommended_pct | -0.05% |\\n\\n**Offered spread over FTP** – *source: query_structured_data*  \\n“The offered spread over FTP (Funds Transfer Pricing) for this deal is **1.70%**. This is calculated by subtracting the internal funding cost/FTP rate (`funding_cost_pct_treasury`: 5.55%) from the final approved price (`final_approved_price_pct`: 7.25%).”\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Pricing‑floor rule for A‑rated AED corporate loans** – *source: query_knowledge_base (FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4, Section\\u202f3.1, Table\\u202f3.1)*  \\n\\n- Tenor ≤\\u202f1\\u202fYear: **85\\u202fbps** over FTP  \\n- Tenor 1‑3\\u202fYears: **105\\u202fbps** over FTP  \\n- Tenor 3‑5\\u202fYears: **130\\u202fbps** over FTP  \\n- Tenor\\u202f>\\u202f5\\u202fYears: **165\\u202fbps** over FTP  \\n\\n*Additional note (Section\\u202f2.4):* “The required margin may be reduced by **up to 25\\u202fbps** from these standard floors if the client demonstrates documented cross‑sell revenues exceeding AED\\u202f500,000 per annum, subject to credit‑authority approval.”\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Compliance Verdict\\n\\n- **Applicable floor:** CUST002’s loan has a tenor of 12\\u202fmonths (≤\\u202f1\\u202fYear) → floor = **85\\u202fbps**.  \\n- **Maximum allowed reduction:** 85\\u202fbps\\u202f‑\\u202f25\\u202fbps = **60\\u202fbps** (if relationship‑value adjustment is approved).  \\n- **Offered spread:** **170\\u202fbps** (1.70\\u202f%).  \\n\\n**Result:** **Compliant** – the offered spread of 170\\u202fbps is well above both the standard floor (85\\u202fbps) and the most permissive adjusted floor (60\\u202fbps). No pricing exception is required.'}]}"}
