FTP** (plus a 40 bps commitment fee floor on undrawn amounts). `[FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4 · Section 3.2]`\\n\\nLet me know if you need help calculating the current all-in rate using live FTP benchmarks or drafting a Pricing Exception request.\"}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-06-29T15:00:57+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "b79421b34fff9c7da639b2e589587167", "span_id": "2ce73529aeb38255", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "C87024D0", "msg": "{'role': 'assistant', 'parts': [{'type': 'text', 'content': 'To assess compliance we need the **offered spread (in\\u202fbps) over the applicable USD FTP rate** for the loan you are pricing for\\u202fCUST\\u202f002.\\n\\n- **Rating:**\\u202fBB  \\n- **Currency:**\\u202fUSD  \\n- **Tenor:**\\u202f18\\u202fmonths\\u202f( falls in the\\u202f1\\u202f–\\u202f3\\u202fyear bucket)  \\n\\n**Pricing‑floor for a BB‑rated USD corporate loan (1\\u202f–\\u202f3\\u202fyr):\\u202f210\\u202fbps over FTP**  \\n*Source: FAB\\u202fCredit\\u202fPricing\\u202fPolicy\\u202fv2.4 – Section\\u202f3, Table\\u202f3.1*  \\n\\nPlease provide the spread you plan to offer (e.g.,\\u202f190\\u202fbps,\\u202f225\\u202fbps, etc.). Once I have that figure I can instantly tell you whether the price complies with the policy (or if a relationship‑value adjustment or pricing exception is required).'}]}"}
