thority.  \\n3. The adjustment is reviewed annually to verify that the client continues to generate the required cross‑sell revenue.  \\n\\nThese rules ensure that any discount granted for relationship value is transparent, risk‑aware, and aligned with FAB’s profitability and credit risk objectives.\\nUser: What is the pricing floor for BB-rated AED corporate loans?\\nAssistant: **Pricing Floor for BB‑rated AED Corporate Loans (FAB Credit Pricing Policy\\u202fv2.4 – Section\\u202f3.1, Table\\u202f3.1)**  \\n\\n| Facility Tenor | Minimum Pricing Floor (Spread over FTP) |\\n|----------------|-------------------------------------------|\\n| ≤\\u202f1\\u202fYear       | 165\\u202fbps                                   |\\n| 1\\u202f–\\u202f3\\u202fYears    | 210\\u202fbps                                   |\\n| 3\\u202f–\\u202f5\\u202fYears    | 260\\u202fbps                                   |\\n| >\\u202f5\\u202fYears      | 320\\u202fbps                                   |\\n\\n**Key Policy Points**  \\n\\n- **All‑in Rate Calculation:** The all‑in rate may not fall below **FTP\\u202f+\\u202fthe floor spread** shown above. FTP rates are tenor‑matched and published monthly by Treasury.  \\n- **Relationship Value Adjustment:** If the client contributes material cross‑sell revenue (annual revenue\\u202f>\\u202fAED\\u202f500,000 across the relationship), the floor may be reduced by up to **25\\u202fbps**, subject to credit authority approval.  \\n- **Pricing Exceptions:** Any price below these floors requires a formal Pricing Exception, including commercial rationale, RAROC sensitivity analysis, and tiered committee approval based on the deviation.  \\n\\n**Source:** query_knowledge_base – FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4, Section\\u202f3.1 (Table\\u202f3.1), Sections\\u202f2.4\\u202f&\\u202f6.\\nUser: how can u help me?\\nAssistant: I’m FAB’s **Price\\u202fAssist** – your single point of contact for any pricing‑related banking question.  \\n\\n### What I can do for you\\n| 