{"ts": "2026-07-03T10:15:08+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "c168ad50117db6c1b1b98afb0c087e6c", "span_id": "e747bf2f8fb4b22e", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "BA6A95CC", "msg": "{'role': 'user', 'parts': [{'type': 'text', 'content': '[Conversation so far]\\nUser: What interest rate should I offer to customer CUST001?\\nAssistant: **Customer:** CUST001 – Al\\u202fNoor Trading LLC  \\n**Internal Rating:** BBB  \\n\\n---\\n\\n### Structured Deal Data (Data Layer)\\n\\n| Deal ID | Recommended\\u202fInterest\\u202fRate | Pricing Limits (Policy) |\\n|---------|---------------------------|--------------------------|\\n| DEAL033 | 6.85\\u202f% | Max Discount\\u202f0.5\\u202f% • Policy\\u202fMax\\u202fDiscount\\u202f0.25\\u202f% • Min\\u202fMargin\\u202f1.75\\u202f% • Min\\u202fExpected\\u202fMargin\\u202f0.75\\u202f% |\\n| DEAL040 | 5.50\\u202f% | Max Discount\\u202f0.25\\u202f% • Policy\\u202fMax\\u202fDiscount\\u202f0.25\\u202f% • Min\\u202fMargin\\u202f0.65\\u202f% • Min\\u202fExpected\\u202fMargin\\u202f0.10\\u202f% |\\n| DEAL041 | 6.70\\u202f% | Max Discount\\u202f0.5\\u202f% • Policy\\u202fMax\\u202fDiscount\\u202f0.25\\u202f% • Min\\u202fMargin\\u202f1.75\\u202f% • Min\\u202fExpected\\u202fMargin\\u202f0.75\\u202f% |\\n\\n*Source:* **query_structured_data – customer_360** (fields listed above).  \\n\\n---\\n\\n### Policy Floor for a BBB‑Rated AED Loan (RAG)\\n\\nFAB Credit Pricing Policy\\u202fv2.4 – **Section\\u202f3.1 (Corporate Term Loans)**  \\n\\n| Facility Tenor | Minimum Pricing Floor (Spread over internal FTP) |\\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------|\\n| ≤\\u202f1\\u202fYear       | 115\\u202fbps |\\n| 1\\u202f–\\u202f3\\u202fYears    | 145\\u202fbps |\\n| 3\\u202f–\\u202f5\\u202fYears    | 180\\u202fbps |\\n| >\\u202f5\\u202fYears      | 220\\u202fbps |\\n\\n> **All‑in minimum rate** = FTP\\u202frate\\u202f(\\u200bpublished monthly)\\u202f+\\u202fapplicable spread.  \\n> *Example:* FTP\\u202f=\\u202f4.85\\u202f% for a 4‑year loan → floor\\u202f=\\u202f4.85\\u202f%\\u202f+\\u202f1.80\\u202f%\\u202f=\\u202f**6.65\\u202f%**.  \\n\\n*Source:* **query_knowledge_base – FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4**, Clauses\\u202f3.1 &\\u202f3.2.  \\n\\n---\\n\\n### Compliance Check & Recommendation\\n\\n| Deal ID | Recommended Rate | Assumed Tenor* | Minimum Floor (Spread\\u202f+\\u202fFTP) | Verdict |\\n|---------|------------------|----------------|------------------------------|---------|\\n| DEAL040 | 5.50\\u202f% | 1‑3\\u202fYears | FTP\\u202f+\\u202f145\\u202fbps. If FTP\\u202f≤\\u202f5.35\\u202f% → floor\\u202f≤\\u202f5.50\\u202f% → **Compliant**. | Likely compliant for short‑term facilities where FTP is ≤\\u202f5.35\\u202f%. |\\n| DEAL033 | 6.85\\u202f% | 3‑5\\u202fYears | FTP\\u202f+\\u202f180\\u202fbps. If FTP\\u202f≤\\u202f6.65\\u202f% → floor\\u202f≤\\u202f6.85\\u202f% → **Compliant**. | Compliant for medium‑term loans with FTP ≤\\u202f6.65\\u202f%. |\\n| DEAL041 | 6.70\\u202f% | 3‑5\\u202fYears | Same floor as DEAL033. If FTP\\u202f≤\\u202f6.50\\u202f% → floor\\u202f≤\\u202f6.70\\u202f% → **Compliant**. | Generally compliant; check FTP if it is >\\u202f6.50\\u202f%. |\\n\\n\\\\*Tenor is not stored in the deal record; the appropriate floor depends on the loan’s maturity.  \\n\\n**Recommendation**\\n\\n1. **Determine the intended loan tenor** (e.g., 1–3\\u202fyears, 3–5\\u202fyears).  \\n2. **Retrieve the current AED FTP rate** for that tenor (published by FAB Treasury).  \\n3. **Apply the spread from the policy** (145\\u202fbps for 1‑3\\u202fyr, 180\\u202fbps for 3‑5\\u202fyr, etc.).  \\n4. **Select the lowest recommended rate that meets or exceeds the calculated floor**:  \\n   - For a **short‑term (≤\\u202f3\\u202fyr) loan**, the 5.50\\u202f% rate (DEAL040) is acceptable provided FTP\\u202f≤\\u202f5.35\\u202f%.  \\n   - For a **medium‑term (3‑5\\u202fyr) loan**, the 6.70\\u202f% rate (DEAL041) or 6.85\\u202f% rate (DEAL033) will be compliant if FTP\\u202f≤\\u202f6.50\\u202f%–6.65\\u202f% respectively.  \\n\\nIf the current FTP is higher than the thresholds above, you will need to **offer a higher rate** (e.g., add the required spread to the FTP) to stay within policy limits.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Action Steps for the Banker\\n\\n1. **Ask the client** for the desired loan tenor (or refer to the deal brief).  \\n2. **Check the latest AED FTP rate** for that tenor.  \\n3. **Calculate the minimum all‑in rate** using the spread table.  \\n4. **Offer the recommended rate** that is **at or above** the calculated floor and respects the deal‑specific pricing limits (max discount, min margin).  \\n\\nThis ensures the offer is both **policy‑compliant** and aligned with FAB’s internal pricing recommendations for CUST001.\\nUser: What interest rate should I offer to customer CUST001?\\nAssistant: **Structured Deal Data (source:\\u202fquery_structured_data –\\u202fpricing_recommendation)**  \\n\\n| Deal\\u202fID | Product | Tenor | Recommended\\u202fPrice\\u202f% | Approved\\u202fPrice\\u202f% | Policy\\u202fMax\\u202fDiscount\\u202f% | Policy\\u202fMin\\u202fMargin\\u202f% | Policy\\u202fMin\\u202fExpected\\u202fMargin\\u202f% | Policy\\u202fCompliant |\\n|--------|---------|-------|----------------------|------------------|------------------------|---------------------|------------------------------|-------------------|\\n| DEAL033 | Trade\\u202fFinance\\u202fLC | 6\\u202fM | 6.85\\u202f% | 6.80\\u202f% | 0.25\\u202f% | 1.75\\u202f% | 0.75\\u202f% | **Yes** |\\n| DEAL040 | Corporate\\u202fDeposit | 1\\u202fM | 5.50\\u202f% | 5.45\\u202f% | 0.25\\u202f% | 0.65\\u202f% | 0.10\\u202f% | **No** (margin\\u202f‑0.50\\u202f%\\u202f<\\u202fmin\\u202fexpected\\u202fmargin) |\\n| DEAL041 | Trade\\u202fFinance\\u202fLC | 3\\u202fM | 6.70\\u202f% | 6.50\\u202f% | 0.25\\u202f% | 1.75\\u202f% | 0.75\\u202f% | **Yes** |\\n\\n**Policy Floors & FTP Reference (source:\\u202fquery_knowledge_base –\\u202fFAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4)**  \\n\\n| Tenor bucket | FTP\\u202f% (illustrative,\\u202f2024‑06) | Minimum Pricing Floor\\u202f% (FTP\\u202f+\\u202fSpread) |\\n|--------------|-------------------------------|------------------------------------------|\\n| ≤\\u202f1\\u202fYear (e.g., 1\\u202fM,\\u202f6\\u202fM) | 5.25\\u202f% (1‑M & 3‑M) / 5.40\\u202f% (6‑M) | 1‑Year:\\u202fFTP\\u202f+\\u202f115\\u202fbps → 5.25\\u202f%\\u202f+\\u202f1.15\\u202f%\\u202f=\\u202f**6.40\\u202f%** (1‑M) <br>6‑M:\\u202fFTP\\u202f+\\u202f115\\u202fbps → 5.40\\u202f%\\u202f+\\u202f1.15\\u202f%\\u202f=\\u202f**6.55\\u202f%** |\\n| 1\\u202f–\\u202f3\\u202fYears | 5.25\\u202f% (illustrative) | FTP\\u202f+\\u202f145\\u202fbps → 5.25\\u202f%\\u202f+\\u202f1.45\\u202f%\\u202f=\\u202f**6.70\\u202f%** |\\n| 3\\u202f–\\u202f5\\u202fYears | 5.40\\u202f% (illustrative) | FTP\\u202f+\\u202f180\\u202fbps → 5.40\\u202f%\\u202f+\\u202f1.80\\u202f%\\u202f=\\u202f**7.20\\u202f%** |\\n\\n⚠\\u202fThe FTP figures above are **illustrative (June\\u202f2024) and may be stale**. FAB Treasury publishes the current month’s FTP rates on the internal Treasury pricing portal; the latest confirmed rates must be used for final pricing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Compliance Check\\n\\n| Deal\\u202fID | Tenor | Applicable Floor\\u202f%* | Recommended\\u202fRate\\u202f% | Compliance |\\n|--------|-------|---------------------|--------------------|------------|\\n| DEAL040 | 1\\u202fM (≤\\u202f1\\u202fyr) | 6.40\\u202f% (FTP\\u202f5.25\\u202f%\\u202f+\\u202f115\\u202fbps) | 5.50\\u202f% | **Non‑Compliant** – rate is below floor (and margin below policy). |\\n| DEAL033 | 6\\u202fM (≤\\u202f1\\u202fyr) | 6.55\\u202f% (FTP\\u202f5.40\\u202f%\\u202f+\\u202f115\\u202fbps) | 6.85\\u202f% | **Compliant** – rate ≥ floor and all policy limits satisfied. |\\n| DEAL041 | 3\\u202fM (≤\\u202f1\\u202fyr) | 6.55\\u202f% (FTP\\u202f5.40\\u202f%\\u202f+\\u202f115\\u202fbps) | 6.70\\u202f% | **Compliant** – rate ≥ floor and policy limits satisfied. |\\n\\n\\\\*Floor calculated using the illustrative FTP rates returned by the knowledge base. Replace the illustrative FTP with the **current confirmed FTP** for an exact floor.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recommended Interest Rate to Offer CUST001\\n\\n1. **Confirm the intended loan tenor** (e.g., 1\\u202fM,\\u202f3\\u202fM,\\u202f6\\u202fM).  \\n2. **Obtain the current AED FTP rate** for that tenor from the Treasury portal.  \\n3. **Calculate the minimum all‑in rate** (FTP\\u202f+\\u202fspread from the policy).  \\n\\nBased on the **illustrative FTP**:\\n\\n| Desired Tenor | Minimum Floor\\u202f% | Recommended Offer\\u202f% (from existing deals) |\\n|---------------|-----------------|--------------------------------------------|\\n| 1\\u202fM (≤\\u202f1\\u202fyr)   | 6.40\\u202f%          | **6.85\\u202f%** (DEAL033) – the only rate above the floor. |\\n| 3\\u202fM (≤\\u202f1\\u202fyr)   | 6.55\\u202f%          | **6.70\\u202f%** (DEAL041) – compliant and close to the floor. |\\n| 6\\u202fM (≤\\u202f1\\u202fyr)   | 6.55\\u202f%          | **6.85\\u202f%** (DEAL033) – compliant. |\\n\\n**Thus, the safest offer is the rate already approved for the comparable deal:**\\n\\n- **6.85\\u202f%** for a 6‑month (or any ≤\\u202f1‑year) loan (DEAL033), or  \\n- **6.70\\u202f%** for a 3‑month loan (DEAL041) if a shorter tenor is preferred.\\n\\nIf the client requires a **1‑month loan**, the illustrative floor (6.40\\u202f%) indicates that **6.85\\u202f%** (DEAL033) remains the only compliant rate.\\n\\n> **Action:** Verify the current FTP; if the live FTP is higher than the illustrative values, increase the offered rate accordingly (FTP\\u202f+\\u202frequired spread). This ensures the offer stays **policy‑compliant** and respects the internal margin and discount limits.\\nUser: Explain step by step how the recommended price was calculated for CUST001.\\nAssistant: **Step‑by‑step construction of the recommended interest rates for CUST001 (Al\\u202fNoor Trading\\u202fLLC)**  \\n\\nThe calculation follows the pricing formula defined in FAB’s internal credit pricing framework and then checks the result against the policy‑defined minimum floor for a BBB‑rated AED loan.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1. Data used for the calculation  \\n\\n| Field (source: **query_structured_data – pricing_recommendation**) | DEAL033 | DEAL040 | DEAL041 |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **funding_cost_pct** | 5.40\\u202f% | 5.05\\u202f% | 5.25\\u202f% |\\n| **standard_margin_pct** | 1.25\\u202f% | 0.25\\u202f% | 1.25\\u202f% |\\n| **risk_premium_pct** | 0.45\\u202f% | 0.45\\u202f% | 0.45\\u202f% |\\n| **relationship_discount_pct** | 0.25\\u202f% | 0.25\\u202f% | 0.25\\u202f% |\\n| **recommended_price_pct** (output) | 6.85\\u202f% | 5.50\\u202f% | 6.70\\u202f% |\\n\\n*All other fields (tenor, product, etc.) are shown in the full table above but are not part of the price‑building arithmetic.*\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. Pricing formula applied  \\n\\nThe bank’s pricing engine builds the **recommended price** as:\\n\\n```\\nRecommended Price (%) = Funding Cost\\n                         + Standard Margin\\n                         + Risk Premium\\n                         – Relationship Discount\\n```\\n\\n*The relationship discount is a credit‑line discount granted for the existing client relationship; it is subtracted because it lowers the price offered to the customer.*\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. Calculation for each deal  \\n\\n| Deal | Calculation (step‑by‑step) | Result |\\n|------|----------------------------|--------|\\n| **DEAL033** (Trade Finance LC, 6\\u202fM) | 1️⃣ Funding Cost\\u202f=\\u202f5.40\\u202f%  <br>2️⃣ + Standard Margin\\u202f=\\u202f1.25\\u202f%  →\\u202f6.65\\u202f%  <br>3️⃣ + Risk Premium\\u202f=\\u202f0.45\\u202f%  →\\u202f7.10\\u202f%  <br>4️⃣ – Relationship Discount\\u202f=\\u202f0.25\\u202f%  →\\u202f**6.85\\u202f%** | **6.85\\u202f%** (matches `recommended_price_pct`) |\\n| **DEAL040** (Corporate Deposit, 1\\u202fM) | 1️⃣ Funding Cost\\u202f=\\u202f5.05\\u202f%  <br>2️⃣ + Standard Margin\\u202f=\\u202f0.25\\u202f%  →\\u202f5.30\\u202f%  <br>3️⃣ + Risk Premium\\u202f=\\u202f0.45\\u202f%  →\\u202f5.75\\u202f%  <br>4️⃣ – Relationship Discount\\u202f=\\u202f0.25\\u202f%  →\\u202f**5.50\\u202f%** | **5.50\\u202f%** |\\n| **DEAL041** (Trade Finance LC, 3\\u202fM) | 1️⃣ Funding Cost\\u202f=\\u202f5.25\\u202f%  <br>2️⃣ + Standard Margin\\u202f=\\u202f1.25\\u202f%  →\\u202f6.50\\u202f%  <br>3️⃣ + Risk Premium\\u202f=\\u202f0.45\\u202f%  →\\u202f6.95\\u202f%  <br>4️⃣ – Relationship Discount\\u202f=\\u202f0.25\\u202f%  →\\u202f**6.70\\u202f%** | **6.70\\u202f%** |\\n\\n**Result:** The `recommended_price_pct` shown in the data is exactly the outcome of the above arithmetic for each deal.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 4. Policy floor comparison (to confirm compliance)  \\n\\n**Policy source:** **query_knowledge_base – FAB Credit Pricing Policy v2.4, Section\\u202f3.1 (Corporate Term Loans)**  \\n\\n| Tenor bucket | Minimum spread over internal FTP (bps) |\\n|--------------|----------------------------------------|\\n| ≤\\u202f1\\u202fYear    | 115\\u202fbps |\\n| 1\\u202f–\\u202f3\\u202fYears | 145\\u202fbps |\\n| 3\\u202f–\\u202f5\\u202fYears | 180\\u202fbps |\\n\\n*All‑in minimum rate = FTP\\u202f(percentage) + applicable spread.*\\n\\nThe policy does **not** prescribe a different spread for BBB versus other ratings; the rating influences the allowable maximum discount (0.25\\u202f% in the data) but the floor spread is the same for all corporate term loans.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 5. Example floor calculation (illustrative)  \\n\\nAssume the current AED FTP published by Treasury for the relevant tenor is **5.25\\u202f%** (example figure).  \\n\\n| Deal | Tenor | Applicable spread | Floor = FTP\\u202f+\\u202fSpread | Recommended price vs. floor |\\n|------|-------|-------------------|----------------------|-----------------------------|\\n| DEAL040 | 1\\u202fM (≤\\u202f1\\u202fyr) | 115\\u202fbps | 5.25\\u202f%\\u202f+\\u202f1.15\\u202f% = **6.40\\u202f%** | 5.50\\u202f% **<\\u202f6.40\\u202f%** → **Below floor (non‑compliant)** |\\n| DEAL033 | 6\\u202fM (≤\\u202f1\\u202fyr) | 115\\u202fbps | 5.25\\u202f%\\u202f+\\u202f1.15\\u202f% = **6.40\\u202f%** | 6.85\\u202f% **≥\\u202f6.40\\u202f%** → **Compliant** |\\n| DEAL041 | 3\\u202fM (≤\\u202f1\\u202fyr) | 115\\u202fbps | 5.25\\u202f%\\u202f+\\u202f1.15\\u202f% = **6.40\\u202f%** | 6.70\\u202f% **≥\\u202f6.40\\u202f%** → **Compliant** |\\n\\n*(If the actual FTP for a 3‑month or 6‑month loan differs, replace the illustrative 5.25\\u202f% with the live rate; the floor moves accordingly.)*\\n\\nThe **policy‑compliant flag** in the data (`policy_compliant = 1` for DEAL033 & DEAL041, `0` for DEAL040) reflects exactly this floor comparison together with the margin checks (minimum margin, minimum expected margin, maximum discount).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 6. Summary of how the recommended price is derived  \\n\\n1. **Gather cost components** – funding cost, standard margin, risk premium, and any relationship discount (all stored per‑deal).  \\n2. **Apply the pricing formula** (add the three cost components, subtract the discount).  \\n3. **Obtain the current internal FTP** for the loan’s tenor from Treasury.  \\n4. **Add the policy‑defined spread** (115\\u202fbps, 145\\u202fbps, or 180\\u202fbps) to the FTP to get the **minimum pricing floor**.  \\n5. **Validate** that the recommended price is **≥\\u202ffloor** and that the resulting margin meets the policy minima (min margin, min expected margin) and that the discount does not exceed the policy max (0.25\\u202f%).  \\n6. **Record the outcome** – `policy_compliant = 1` if all checks pass; otherwise flag as non‑compliant.\\n\\nAll numbers presented above are taken verbatim from the two source views:\\n\\n- **Pricing‑recommendation view** (structured deal data) – `query_structured_data`.  \\n- **FAB Credit Pricing Policy v2.4, Section\\u202f3.1** – `query_knowledge_base`.  \\n\\nThese steps explain precisely how the **6.85\\u202f%**, **5.50\\u202f%**, and **6.70\\u202f%** recommended rates for CUST001 were calculated and how compliance with the bank’s pricing policy is assessed.\\n\\n[Current question]\\nCustomer CUST001 has received a lower competitor offer. Should we match, counter, or reject?'}]}"}
