{"ts": "2026-07-03T11:04:08+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "aabb982839cbbb4116861950388c33aa", "span_id": "6b72dbcba5aa58a8", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "4387E4F7", "msg": "{'role': 'user', 'parts': [{'type': 'text', 'content': '[Conversation so far]\\nUser: Customer CUST001 has received a lower competitor offer. Should we match, counter, or reject?\\nAssistant: **CUST001 – Al Noor Trading LLC – Pricing Situation**\\n\\n| Deal | Product | Funding Cost\\u202f% | Recommended\\u202f% | Final Approved\\u202f% | Expected Margin\\u202f% | Policy\\u202fMin\\u202fMargin\\u202f% | Policy\\u202fMin\\u202fExpected\\u202fMargin\\u202f% | Discount\\u202fAllowed\\u202f% (policy) | Policy\\u202fCompliant |\\n|------|---------|----------------|--------------|------------------|-------------------|----------------------|------------------------------|-----------------------------|------------------|\\n| DEAL033 | Trade Finance LC | 5.40 | 6.85 | 6.80 | 1.05 | 1.75 | 0.75 | 0.25 | **Yes** |\\n| DEAL041 | Trade Finance LC | 5.25 | 6.70 | 6.50 | 0.90 | 1.75 | 0.75 | 0.25 | **Yes** |\\n\\n*Source: **pricing_recommendation** (structured data)*  \\n\\n**FAB policy on competitor‑price matching**\\n\\n- Competitor evidence must be provided for any transaction **>\\u202fAED\\u202f25\\u202fmillion**.\\u202f[Source: *FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4 – Section\\u202f2.3*]  \\n- **Maximum discount** that may be applied to the standard pricing floor is **25\\u202fbps (0.25\\u202f%)**.\\u202f[Source: *FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4 – Section\\u202f2.4*]  \\n- The transaction must retain an **expected margin of at least 0.75\\u202f%** (policy_min_expected_margin_pct).\\u202f[Source: *FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4 – Section\\u202f3.1*]  \\n- If a competitor’s offer would force a discount **greater than 0.25\\u202f%** or would push the expected margin **below 0.75\\u202f%**, a **Pricing Exception** must be raised (or the deal rejected).\\u202f[Source: *FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4 – Section\\u202f6*]  \\n\\n---\\n\\n### Recommendation for the current competitor offer\\n\\n1. **Determine the competitor’s quoted price** for the same product, tenor and amount.  \\n2. **Compare it with FAB’s current approved price** (6.80\\u202f% for DEAL033; 6.50\\u202f% for DEAL041).\\n\\n| Scenario | Action | Reasoning |\\n|----------|--------|-----------|\\n| **Competitor price ≥\\u202f6.55\\u202f%** (i.e., no more than **0.25\\u202f%** cheaper than FAB’s approved price) | **Match** the competitor’s price (or stay at the approved price). | Discount stays within the **0.25\\u202f%** limit and expected margin remains **≥\\u202f0.75\\u202f%** – fully compliant. |\\n| **Competitor price between 6.55\\u202f% and 6.30\\u202f%** (discount **>\\u202f0.25\\u202f%** but still above the policy floor) | **Counter** with the best price you can offer that respects the **0.25\\u202f%** discount cap (i.e., 6.55\\u202f% for DEAL033, 6.25\\u202f% for DEAL041). | Keeps the deal compliant; shows willingness to be competitive while adhering to policy. |\\n| **Competitor price <\\u202f6.30\\u202f%** (discount exceeds policy limits or would drive expected margin\\u202f<\\u202f0.75\\u202f%) | **Reject** the request to match or **escalate** for a **Pricing Exception**. | Policy explicitly forbids pricing below the floor without an exception; proceeding would be non‑compliant. |\\n\\n### Practical next steps\\n\\n1. **Obtain the exact competitor offer** (include documentation/evidence).  \\n2. If the offer is within the **0.25\\u202f%** discount band, approve a match.  \\n3. If the offer exceeds that band but is still viable, propose a **counter‑offer** at the maximum allowable discount (0.25\\u202f%).  \\n4. If the offer is lower than the allowable discount, **initiate a Pricing Exception** (Section\\u202f6) or politely decline, citing policy constraints.\\n\\n**Bottom line:**  \\n- **Match** only when the competitor price is ≤\\u202f0.25\\u202f% cheaper than FAB’s approved price.  \\n- **Counter** with the 0.25\\u202f% discount ceiling when the competitor is cheaper but still above the floor.  \\n- **Reject / seek exception** when the competitor’s price would breach the discount limit or push the expected margin below 0.75\\u202f%.\\nUser: What interest rate should I offer to customer CUST001?\\nAssistant: **Pricing recommendation for customer\\u202fCUST001 (Al\\u202fNoor Trading\\u202fLLC)**  \\n\\n| Deal ID | Product | Recommended\\u202fInterest\\u202fRate\\u202f% | Final\\u202fApproved\\u202fRate\\u202f% | Expected\\u202fMargin\\u202f% | Policy\\u202fMin\\u202fMargin\\u202f% | Max\\u202fDiscount\\u202fAllowed\\u202f% (policy) |\\n|---------|---------|----------------------------|-----------------------|-------------------|----------------------|---------------------------------|\\n| DEAL033 | Trade Finance\\u202fLC | **6.85\\u202f%** | 6.80\\u202f% | 1.05\\u202f% | 1.75\\u202f% | 0.50\\u202f% |\\n| DEAL040 | Trade Finance\\u202fLC | **5.50\\u202f%** | 5.45\\u202f% | –0.50\\u202f% | 0.65\\u202f% | 0.25\\u202f% |\\n| DEAL041 | Trade Finance\\u202fLC | **6.70\\u202f%** | 6.50\\u202f% | 0.90\\u202f% | 1.75\\u202f% | 0.50\\u202f% |\\n\\n*Source: **query_structured_data** – “pricing recommendation data for customer CUST001”*  \\n\\n---\\n\\n### Policy floor for Trade Finance Letter of Credit (BB‑rated customer)\\n\\nThe knowledge‑base lookup returned the following policy statement:\\n\\n> *“FAB pricing policy floor for Trade Finance Letter of Credit product for a customer with rating BB.”*  \\n\\n*Source: **query_knowledge_base** – “FAB pricing policy floor for Trade Finance Letter of Credit product for a customer with rating BB”*  \\n\\n> **⚠\\u202fNote:** The knowledge‑base response did not contain the numeric floor value (the passage is incomplete/unstale). To verify compliance you will need the exact floor percentage for a BB‑rated Trade Finance LC.  \\n\\n---\\n\\n### What rate should you **offer**?\\n\\n1. **Use the recommended rate** shown above for each deal, **provided it is not below the policy floor** (which must be confirmed).  \\n2. The recommended rates already respect the internal “max discount allowed” limits (0.25\\u202f%‑0.50\\u202f% depending on the deal) and are above the policy minimum margin where that margin is positive.  \\n3. For **DEAL040**, the expected margin is negative (‑0.50\\u202f%). Since the policy‑minimum margin for this deal is 0.65\\u202f%, the current recommendation would be **non‑compliant** unless an exception is obtained or the rate is adjusted upward.  \\n\\n**Verdict per deal (based on available data):**  \\n\\n| Deal ID | Compliance Verdict | Reason |\\n|---------|-------------------|--------|\\n| DEAL033 | **Compliant** | Recommended rate 6.85\\u202f% ≤ max discount 0.50\\u202f% and expected margin 1.05\\u202f% ≥ policy min margin 1.75\\u202f% (margin‑based compliance is satisfied). |\\n| DEAL040 | **Non‑Compliant** | Expected margin (‑0.50\\u202f%) is below policy‑min‑margin (0.65\\u202f%). Requires price adjustment or exception. |\\n| DEAL041 | **Compliant** | Expected margin 0.90\\u202f% ≥ policy‑min‑expected‑margin (0.75\\u202f%) and discount within allowed 0.50\\u202f%. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Recommended action  \\n\\n- **DEAL033 & DEAL041:** Offer the **recommended rates** (6.85\\u202f% and 6.70\\u202f% respectively).  \\n- **DEAL040:** Either raise the offered rate to meet the minimum margin requirement (e.g., increase to at least 5.65\\u202f% to achieve a 0.65\\u202f% margin) or submit a **Pricing Exception** request.  \\n\\n*If you obtain the exact policy floor percentage for a BB‑rated Trade Finance LC, compare it with the recommended rates above to confirm final compliance.*\\nUser: Explain step by step how the recommended price was calculated for CUST001.\\nAssistant: **Step‑by‑step calculation of the **Recommended\\u202fPrice\\u202f%** for each CUST001 deal**  \\n\\n---\\n\\n### Sources  \\n\\n| Data | Source |\\n|------|--------|\\n| Deal‑level numbers (funding cost, standard margin, risk premium, relationship discount, recommended price, etc.) | **query_structured_data** – “pricing recommendation data for customer CUST001” |\\n| Pricing‑methodology description (how the components are combined) | **query_knowledge_base** – “FAB pricing calculation methodology for recommended price: funding cost, standard margin, risk premium, relationship discount” – *FAB\\u202fCredit\\u202fPricing\\u202fPolicy\\u202fv2.4\\u202f·\\u202fSection\\u202f2.1‑2.2* |\\n\\n> **Knowledge‑base passage** (exact wording):  \\n\\n> “The methodology combines your three referenced components—**Funding Cost**, **Standard Margin**, **Risk Premium**, and **Relationship Discount**—into a structured pricing framework.”  \\n\\n> “**Recommended Price** is derived by adding the Funding Cost, Standard Margin and Risk Premium, then subtracting any approved Relationship Discount.”  \\n\\n> *(Source: FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4 – Section\\u202f2.1,\\u202f2.2)*  \\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Deal\\u202fDEAL033 (Trade Finance\\u202fLC)\\n\\n| Component | Value from structured data | Calculation |\\n|-----------|---------------------------|-------------|\\n| Funding Cost (FTP) | 5.40\\u202f% | — |\\n| Standard Margin | 1.25\\u202f% | — |\\n| Risk Premium | 0.45\\u202f% | — |\\n| Relationship Discount (approved) | 0.25\\u202f% | — |\\n| **Recommended Price** | 6.85\\u202f% | **5.40\\u202f% + 1.25\\u202f% + 0.45\\u202f% – 0.25\\u202f% = 6.85\\u202f%** |\\n\\n*Result matches the **recommended_price_pct** field returned by the data layer.*\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Deal\\u202fDEAL040 (Corporate Deposit)\\n\\n| Component | Value | Calculation |\\n|-----------|-------|-------------|\\n| Funding Cost | 5.05\\u202f% | — |\\n| Standard Margin | 0.25\\u202f% | — |\\n| Risk Premium | 0.45\\u202f% | — |\\n| Relationship Discount | 0.25\\u202f% | — |\\n| **Recommended Price** | 5.50\\u202f% | **5.05\\u202f% + 0.25\\u202f% + 0.45\\u202f% – 0.25\\u202f% = 5.50\\u202f%** |\\n\\n*Result matches the **recommended_price_pct** field for DEAL040.*\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Deal\\u202fDEAL041 (Trade Finance\\u202fLC)\\n\\n| Component | Value | Calculation |\\n|-----------|-------|-------------|\\n| Funding Cost | 5.25\\u202f% | — |\\n| Standard Margin | 1.25\\u202f% | — |\\n| Risk Premium | 0.45\\u202f% | — |\\n| Relationship Discount | 0.25\\u202f% | — |\\n| **Recommended Price** | 6.70\\u202f% | **5.25\\u202f% + 1.25\\u202f% + 0.45\\u202f% – 0.25\\u202f% = 6.70\\u202f%** |\\n\\n*Result matches the **recommended_price_pct** field for DEAL041.*\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Summary of the calculation logic\\n\\n1. **Retrieve the numeric components** for the deal from the structured pricing‑recommendation record (funding_cost_pct, standard_margin_pct, risk_premium_pct, relationship_discount_pct).  \\n2. **Apply the policy‑defined formula** (Funding Cost\\u202f+\\u202fStandard Margin\\u202f+\\u202fRisk Premium\\u202f−\\u202fRelationship Discount) as described in the FAB Credit Pricing Policy (Section\\u202f2.1‑2.2).  \\n3. **The output of the formula is the Recommended Price** (recommended_price_pct).  \\n4. **Compare the calculated figure with the stored recommended_price_pct** to confirm correctness; all three deals align exactly, indicating the system applied the methodology consistently.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Result:** The recommended rates shown in the pricing‑recommendation dataset (6.85\\u202f% for DEAL033, 5.50\\u202f% for DEAL040, 6.70\\u202f% for DEAL041) are each the sum of the funding cost, standard margin, and risk premium, minus the approved relationship discount, exactly as prescribed by FAB’s pricing methodology.\\nUser: Which deals are non-compliant and why?\\nAssistant: **Non‑compliant deal(s) for customer\\u202fCUST001**\\n\\n| Deal ID | Reason for non‑compliance | Key figures (from **pricing_recommendation**) |\\n|---------|---------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|\\n| **DEAL040** | **Expected margin is below the policy‑minimum expected margin** | •\\u202fExpected\\u202fmargin\\u202f% **‑0.50**  <br>•\\u202fPolicy\\u202fminimum\\u202fexpected\\u202fmargin\\u202f% **0.10** (field *policy_min_expected_margin_pct*) <br>•\\u202fMargin‑below‑min flag **1** (field *margin_below_min*) |\\n|            | (All other checks are satisfied) | •\\u202fDiscount\\u202fexceeds\\u202fpolicy\\u202f? **No** (field *discount_exceeds_policy* = 0) <br>•\\u202fPrice\\u202fbelow\\u202fpolicy\\u202ffloor\\u202f? **No** (field *price_below_policy_floor* = 0) <br>•\\u202fPolicy‑compliant flag **0** (field *policy_compliant* = 0) |\\n\\n**Why DEAL040 fails**\\n\\n- The FAB Credit Pricing Policy requires that every transaction achieve at least a **minimum expected margin** (the “expected margin” after applying the final approved price).  \\n- For **Corporate Deposit** (product\\u202fPROD008) the policy‑minimum expected margin recorded in the data is **0.10\\u202f%**.  \\n- DEAL040’s calculated expected margin is **‑0.50\\u202f%**, which is **0.60\\u202f% below** the required minimum, triggering the *margin_below_min* flag.  \\n- Because the margin condition is not met, the deal is flagged **non‑compliant** even though the discount (0.25\\u202f%) and price‑floor checks are within limits.\\n\\n**All other deals for CUST001 are compliant**\\n\\n| Deal ID | Compliance verdict | Reason |\\n|---------|-------------------|--------|\\n| DEAL033 | **Compliant** | Expected margin\\u202f1.05\\u202f%\\u202f≥\\u202fpolicy\\u202fminimum\\u202fexpected\\u202fmargin\\u202f0.75\\u202f%; discount\\u202f0\\u202f% ≤ policy max\\u202f0.25\\u202f%; price not below floor. |\\n| DEAL041 | **Compliant** | Expected margin\\u202f0.90\\u202f%\\u202f≥\\u202fpolicy\\u202fminimum\\u202fexpected\\u202fmargin\\u202f0.75\\u202f%; discount\\u202f0\\u202f% ≤ policy max\\u202f0.25\\u202f%; price not below floor. |\\n\\n**Sources**\\n\\n- Structured pricing‑recommendation record for **CUST001** (fields shown above).  \\n- Policy‑minimum expected‑margin requirement (from the knowledge base) – *unavailable* (the knowledge‑base query returned **RAG_UNAVAILABLE**). Consequently, the numeric policy threshold used in the table comes from the *policy_min_expected_margin_pct* field in the structured data.  \\n\\n**Summary**\\n\\n- **Only DEAL040 is non‑compliant**, because its expected margin (‑0.50\\u202f%) falls short of the policy‑required minimum expected margin (0.10\\u202f%).  \\n- To bring DEAL040 into compliance, the bank must either **increase the offered rate** to raise the expected margin to at least 0.10\\u202f% (e.g., adjust the final approved price upward) or **obtain a Pricing Exception** as defined in the FAB Credit Pricing Policy.\\n\\n[Current question]\\nhow about for cust002, cust003? compare all those in a single table side by side on all the aspects... keep it simple\\n\\nCRITICAL: Your previous response contained placeholder text like [Name] or [Value] that is NOT real data. You MUST call the tool, then copy the EXACT values it returns — customer names, figures, percentages — verbatim. NEVER invent or template any field.'}]}"}
