{"ts": "2026-07-03T13:46:32+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "76716a21c678ab2a5a0f3c0a75a766aa", "span_id": "993b8536fa52e2df", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "9739E7AC", "msg": "{'role': 'tool', 'parts': [{'type': 'tool_call_response', 'id': 'fc_13806f3c-1a72-4534-8f32-71384a63366e', 'response': 'Based on the FAB Credit Pricing Policy (FAB-POL-PRICE-2024-v2.4), the recommended loan pricing methodology for Corporate and Commercial Banking is governed by four core principles and follows a structured, step-by-step calculation to ensure full cost recovery and risk-adjusted profitability. \\n\\n*Note: This methodology applies to corporate, commercial, and syndicated lending. Retail lending is governed by a separate policy (FAB-POL-PRICE-RETAIL-2024).*\\n\\n### 1. Core Pricing Principles\\nBefore calculating a price, the transaction must satisfy these four principles simultaneously [source: FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4 · Section 2]:\\n*   **Cost Recovery:** The price must fully cover Funds Transfer Pricing (FTP), capital costs, operating costs, and expected credit losses.\\n*   **Risk-Adjusted Profitability:** The loan must generate a Risk-Adjusted Return on Capital (RAROC) exceeding FAB\\'s hurdle rate (currently **13.5% post-tax**).\\n*   **Market Competitiveness:** Pricing must be benchmarked against peer banks and public rates for facilities over AED 25M.\\n*   **Relationship Value:** Long-term profitability across the entire client relationship can justify strategic pricing adjustments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. Step-by-Step Calculation Methodology\\n\\n#### Step 1: Determine the Funds Transfer Price (FTP)\\nFAB Treasury sets the internal cost of funds on a matched-maturity basis, published monthly. \\n*   **Components:** Market Base Rate (e.g., SOFR/EIBOR) + Liquidity Premium + Tenor Premium.\\n*   *Example:* A 3–5 year tenor bucket carries a liquidity premium of 35 bps and a tenor premium of 25 bps over the 12-month EIBOR rate [source: FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4 · Section 4.1].\\n\\n#### Step 2: Calculate Minimum Cost Recovery\\nAdd the allocated risk and operational costs to the FTP to establish a baseline break-even rate:\\n> **Minimum Rate = FTP Rate + Capital Cost (bps) + Operating Cost Allocation (bps) + Expected Credit Loss Provision (bps)** [source: FAB_Credit_Pricing_Policy_v2.4 · Section 2.1]\\n\\n#### Step 3: Apply Credit Spread (Pricing Floor)\\nApply a risk-based spread based on the client’s **Internal Credit Rating** and **Facility Tenor**. These act as the absolute minimum floor below which no transaction can proceed without an exception:\\n| Client Rating | Tenor 1-3 Years | Tenor 3-5 Years |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **AAA / AA** | 80 bps | 100 bps |\\n| **A** | 105 bps | 130 bps |\\n| **BBB** | 145 bps | 180 bps |\\n| **BB** | 210 bps | 260 bps |\\n| **B** | 300 bps | 370 bps |\\n*Credited to Section 3.1 of the Pricing Policy.*\\n\\n#### Step 4: Add Front-End & Recurring Fees\\nFor products like Corporate Term Loans (CTLs), calculate the final \"All-In Rate\" by adding:\\n*   **Arrangement Fee:** Typical range of 30–100 bps of the facility amount (upfront).\\n*   **Commitment Fee:** Typical standard of 35% of the applicable margin on undrawn portions.\\n*   *Note:* All fees are annualized when calculated for profitability metrics [source: FAB_Corporate_Term_Loan_Product_Manual_v2.0 · Section 3.1].\\n\\n#### Step 5: Validate RAROC Hurdle\\nVerify that the proposed All-In Rate meets the 13.5% threshold:\\n'}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-07-03T13:46:36+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "76716a21c678ab2a5a0f3c0a75a766aa", "span_id": "993b8536fa52e2df", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "9739E7AC", "msg": "{'role': 'assistant', 'parts': [{'type': 'text', 'content': '<llm_reasoning>{\"phase\":\"intent_routing\",\"intent\":\"hybrid\",\"data_signals\":[\"recommended price\",\"CUST001\"],\"rag_signals\":[\"pricing methodology\",\"recommended loan pricing\"],\"rationale\":\"User asks how the recommended price for a specific customer was calculated, requiring the actual price (structured data) and the pricing calculation steps (knowledge base)\",\"confidence\":0.98}</llm_reasoning>\\n\\n**Recommended price for CUST001**  \\nSource: query_structured_data – *DATA_UNAVAILABLE (no price record returned for CUST001).*\\n\\n**Pricing methodology – step‑by‑step calculation**  \\nSource: query_knowledge_base – FAB Credit Pricing Policy (FAB‑POL‑PRICE‑2024‑v2.4) – Section\\u202f2,\\u202f3.1,\\u202f4.1; FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual (v2.0) – Section\\u202f3.1.\\n\\n> **Core Pricing Principles** (Section\\u202f2)  \\n> *Cost Recovery, Risk‑Adjusted Profitability, Market Competitiveness, Relationship Value.*  \\n\\n> **Step\\u202f1 – Determine the Funds Transfer Price (FTP)** (Section\\u202f4.1)  \\n> FTP = Market Base Rate (e.g., 12‑month EIBOR) + Liquidity Premium + Tenor Premium.  \\n> Example: 3–5\\u202fyear bucket → Liquidity Premium\\u202f=\\u202f35\\u202fbps, Tenor Premium\\u202f=\\u202f25\\u202fbps.  \\n\\n> **Step\\u202f2 – Calculate Minimum Cost Recovery** (Section\\u202f2.1)  \\n> Minimum Rate = FTP + Capital Cost (bps) + Operating Cost Allocation (bps) + Expected Credit Loss Provision (bps).  \\n\\n> **Step\\u202f3 – Apply Credit Spread (Pricing Floor)** (Section\\u202f3.1)  \\n\\n| Client Rating | Tenor\\u202f1‑3\\u202fYears | Tenor\\u202f3‑5\\u202fYears |\\n|---------------|----------------|----------------|\\n| AAA / AA      | 80\\u202fbps         | 100\\u202fbps |\\n| A             | 105\\u202fbps        | 130\\u202fbps |\\n| BBB           | 145\\u202fbps        | 180\\u202fbps |\\n| BB            | 210\\u202fbps        | 260\\u202fbps |\\n| B             | 300\\u202fbps        | 370\\u202fbps |\\n\\n> **Step\\u202f4 – Add Front‑End & Recurring Fees** (Corporate Term Loan Product Manual, Section\\u202f3.1)  \\n> • Arrangement Fee: 30–100\\u202fbps of facility amount (up‑front).  \\n> • Commitment Fee: 35\\u202f% of the applicable margin on undrawn portions (annualized).  \\n\\n> **Step\\u202f5 – Validate RAROC Hurdle** (Section\\u202f2)  \\n> Compute the all‑in rate; ensure the resulting Risk‑Adjusted Return on Capital (RAROC) exceeds the FAB hurdle rate of **13.5\\u202f% post‑tax**.  \\n\\n**How the calculation would be applied to CUST001**  \\n1. Retrieve CUST001’s internal credit rating and facility tenor.  \\n2. Obtain the current FTP components (EIBOR, liquidity, tenor premiums).  \\n3. Add capital, operating, and expected loss costs to FTP to get the minimum rate.  \\n4. Apply the rating‑tenor spread from the table above as a floor.  \\n5. Add any applicable arrangement and commitment fees.  \\n6. Calculate the all‑in rate and test against the 13.5\\u202f% RAROC threshold.  \\n7. The resulting all‑in rate becomes the **recommended price** (if data were available).  \\n\\nSince the specific recommended price for CUST001 is not available in the structured data source, the above steps describe exactly how FAB derives that price.\\n\\n<llm_reasoning>{\"phase\":\"synthesis\",\"sources_used\":[\"query_structured_data\",\"query_knowledge_base\"],\"key_findings\":[\"Structured data for CUST001\\'s recommended price is unavailable\",\"Knowledge base provides the full FAB pricing methodology and fee structure\"],\"answer_rationale\":\"Combined the unavailability notice with the complete, verbatim policy steps to explain how the price would be calculated for CUST001\"}<\\\\/llm_reasoning>'}]}"}
